==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat God the Awesome''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cat God the Golden''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Since Cat God the Great is a Special Cat, he can be used on {{4c}} stages or [[:Category:Li'l Stages|Li'l Stages]] as a backline support unit. In comparison with [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]], he is cheaper and guaranteed to [[Knockback]] enemies twice with the first two hits, but his attack rate and standing range are far, far inferior, resulting in much lower overall DPS. His very long cooldown (comparable to most Ubers in the [[Tales of the Nekoluga (Gacha Event)|Tales of the Nekoluga]] banner at nearly 5 minutes) makes him difficult to replace during fights, and in regards to his [[Omni Strike]] ability, he is able to knock burrowed [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] back into himself (although he isn't useful on Zombie stages to begin with). On the other hand, he can make great use of his '''850''' range Omni Strike since such units stand at their maximum range to enemy bases. With proper tactics, this can be used to cheese certain stages, such as [[Tiny Meows (Deadly)|Tiny Meows]] and [[Tiny Will (Deadly)|Tiny Will]].

==='''True Form'''===
Cat God the Golden gains 1% more health and the Money Up ability. The miniscule health increase (only adding 255 health at level 30) is irrelevant and does nothing for the unit, and the Money Up is a minor addition and generally sees very little use, if any at all. As Gold Catfruit are incredibly rare and typically require large amounts of XP or significant game progression to obtain, this True Form is ill-advised unless players have nowhere to spend XP/Gold Catfruit and would like his [[True Form]] for collection purposes, or to unlock and invest in his talents.

==='''Talents'''===
Despite being a fairly underwhelming unit even with Talents (primarily due to his long attack cycle), Cat God's performance still shouldn't be dismissed.

'''Attack Buff''' is the most notable of the bunch. Although Cat God's DPS is horrendous, the fact he receives an 80% boost (in line with Special units that have talents, as opposed to the 20% for most other units) makes it much more appealing combined with his high damage on his third hit and his far-reaching Omni Strike that brings forth devastation from extreme range. At level 50 he has around 150,000 damage on his final hit with this Talent maxed, enough to eliminate a variety of peons, and allowing his [[Money Up]] ability to yield large amounts of income.

'''[[Dodge]]''' is a similar story to [[Mola King (Uber Rare Cat)|Master of the Pacific]]. 50% Dodge Chance for up to 2 seconds when fully upgraded is very inconsistent for such a fragile unit, as he is unlikely to survive any direct confrontations, but it's still unusually high compared to other dodge-based units. This Talent mainly serves as assurance in the case of a stray attack (such as a Death Surge) hits him, as he might evade it and continue fighting.

'''[[Weaken]]''' further improves Cat God's potential as a support unit, since it lasts for 5 seconds. Being able to apply both it and Knockback to essentially whole field greatly improves his ability to hinder frontline threats. Much like [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultima Galaxy Cosmo]]'s Freeze and Knockback versus his targeted traits, Cat God's Weaken has poor uptime due to his attack rate, yet creates an opening that other units may exploit.

'''[[Immune to Curse|Curse Immunity]]''', while not as essential as the others, is still important to have. Granted, Cat God cannot survive various Curse-inflicting attacks, but there may be cases where he would face off the Relic Doge Base, which comes with negligible damage and a Curse effect with high uptime. As his Curse-vulnerable abilities (Dodge/Weaken/Knockback) are just as valuable as his range, this enables him to continue supporting the frontlines even in its presence.

'''Defense Buff''' generally should be the last of the player's concerns. As with other Special Units, it offers a large 80% increase to his health instead of the usual 20%, allowing him to fare much better when under fire, but much like Dodge, only partially compensates for his fragility, as he relies heavily on his Omni Strikes and other units to keep himself safe.

